 \operatorname{IndCoh}(\Omega_{\mathcal{X}}) \to  \operatorname{IndCoh}(\Omega_{\mathcal{X}})  
\end{align}
where $\Delta \colon \mathcal{X} \to \mathcal{X} \times \mathcal{X}$ is the diagonal.

For $\mathcal{E} \in \operatorname{IndCoh}(\Omega_{\mathcal{X}})$, we define 
\begin{align*}
    \mathrm{Supp}^L(\mathcal{E}) \subset \mathfrak{g}/G
\end{align*}
to be the support of $\mathcal{E}$ with respect to the above 
$\operatorname{QCoh}^{{\mathbin{\mkern-6mu\fatslash}}}(\mathfrak{g}/G)$-action, i.e. 
the support of the inner homomorphism 
